# /sdd-status

Purpose:
  Auto-generated purpose for sdd-status.

Owns: commands\sdd-status.sdd
Description:
  Show current execution status: token usage, decisions, tasks, and
  pending approvals.

Usage:
  /sdd-status
  /sdd-status --tokens
  /sdd-status --decisions

Options:
  --tokens     Show detailed token usage per stage
  --decisions  Show decision status

Output:
  Markdown table: stage, tokens used, status, next step.

Rules:
  [STATUS-01] /sdd-status MUST NOT modify any files — read-only operation.
  [STATUS-02] /sdd-status MUST resolve @references via INDEX.sdd routing.
  [STATUS-03] /sdd-status MUST display current execution context.

